{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-runtime","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes sourced Bash libraries, traps, globals, and set -euo behavior across runtime scripts.","prompt_body":"Review the Bash execution semantics in the changed scripts, especially source-time versus run-time behavior, global variable initialization, traps, mktemp cleanup, and Bash 3.2 compatibility. Check whether functions behave correctly when scripts are sourced by harnesses and later executed directly. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"release-state","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Release Step 7/8 now depends on root resolution, captured upgrade output, and persisted state across separate fences.","prompt_body":"Examine the /release Step 7 and Step 8 flow for correctness of active root resolution, fallback behavior, output parsing, and release-step7.env persistence. Pay special attention to whether state survives between documented shell snippets and whether restart decisions cover same-version cone repairs without false positives. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sparse-cone","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The change introduces a shared sparse allowlist contract and separates script root from installed plugin root.","prompt_body":"Assess the sparse checkout architecture, including the new single source of truth for LARCH_SPARSE_DIRS, normalization behavior, and SCRIPT_ROOT versus PLUGIN_ROOT separation. Look for places where the allowlist might still be read from a stale installed cache root or where marketplace clone path binding could use the wrong HOME. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"hook-failopen","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"SessionStart drift probing must remain advisory, non-mutating, cwd-independent, and fail-open under stripped environments.","prompt_body":"Review the SessionStart sparse-cone drift probe for fail-open behavior under set -euo pipefail, missing HOME, missing git, missing libraries, empty comparison inputs, and stripped hook environments. Verify that the probe is non-mutating, cwd-independent, and only appends advisories from the parent shell when appropriate. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-hermeticity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan calls out prior harness hazards around HOME isolation and source order that could mutate developer state or create vacuous tests.","prompt_body":"Inspect the changed harnesses for hermetic setup, especially HOME isolation before sourcing upgrade-larch.sh, marketplace fixture placement, and reapplication of overridden globals after re-sourcing. Check whether the tests genuinely exercise root resolution, cone drift detection, and script-root allowlist behavior rather than comparing the library against itself. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
